6. This Court has considered following aspects,
(i) prima facie, the dispute seems to be of civil nature as the same is out of some business transactions, however, the aforesaid observations are prima facie in nature;
(ii) no civil remedy for recovery of outstanding amount is exhausted by the complainant;
(iii) learned advocate Mr.Suraj Shukla opposed the application on the ground that there are past antecedents against the present applicants.
(iv) however, learned advocate Mr.Majmudar, countering the aforesaid submission by submitting that the present applicants are seeking only anticipatory bail, and even if, R/CR.MA/15839/2022 ORDER DATED: 21/04/2023 there are past antecedents, the proceedings would remain, and ultimately if the evidence goes against the present applicants at the end of trial, the Court has an ample power to punish the present applicants, if they found guilty;
(v) pursuant to the interim order dated 30.08.2022, the applicants appeared before the Investigating Officer, and which shows that they are cooperating with the investigation.
7.

The applicants are ordered to be released on bail in the event of their arrest in connection with FIR C.R.No.11210046220992 of 2022 registered with Puna Taluka Police Station, Dist. Surat on executing a personal bond of Rs.10,000/- (Rupees Ten Thousand Only) each with one surety each of like amount on the following conditions:
(a) shall cooperate with the investigation and make themselves available for interrogation whenever required;
